Credits

The permission model of warden -- groups with a numeric level, named
permissions granted to groups, a per-group vehicle cap, the rank rule that an
action needs a higher level than its target -- follows the semantics of
CobaltEssentials, a server plugin for another BeamNG multiplayer platform,
released under the GNU General Public License version 3 by its authors
(https://github.com/prestonelam2003/CobaltEssentials). No source code of
CobaltEssentials is included in warden; the semantics were reimplemented for
NodeMP's API, identity model and storage.

The in-game panel was written from scratch. Its control model and window
structure -- a window shown by default whose per-player state the server
keeps, a chat command and a bindable game action that toggle it, a QuickInfo
bar with status marks, a UI scale with a reset, the tabs Players / Config /
Environment / Database, a collapsing header per player with a row of small
buttons and the tree nodes vehicles / info / permissions -- reproduce the
arrangement of CobaltEssentialsInterface by Stanley Dudek
(https://github.com/StanleyDudek/CobaltEssentialsInterface), the interface
for CobaltEssentials on the other platform, as a usability reference. That
project publishes no licence, so nothing of it -- code, strings, colour
values or other constants -- was copied; the behaviour was reimplemented
against NodeMP's client mod and Dear ImGui binding.
